---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro'
import { contact } from '../data/site'
---

<Base title="Privacy policy | Tessera" description="How Tessera handles your information: scans stay on your computer, no analytics, no tracking.">
  <Prose title="Privacy policy" intro="Effective 26 November 2026. Tessera is offered by Beyond Enterprises. This policy describes what the app and this website actually do.">
    <h2>Your files stay on your computer</h2>
    <p>To build its storage map, Tessera reads the names, sizes, dates and attributes of files and folders on your computer. That information stays on your computer and is never uploaded.</p>
    <p>When you use Duplicates, Tessera reads the contents of files of 1 MB and larger to compare them. This happens only on your computer. Files that are stored online only (for example in OneDrive or iCloud Drive) are never opened, so nothing is downloaded.</p>

    <h2>What Tessera stores on your computer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your preferences, such as theme and how sizes are shown.</li>
      <li>Your Pro licence activation, kept in Windows Credential Manager or the macOS Keychain.</li>
      <li>A "Recently moved" list of items Tessera moved to the Recycle Bin or Trash (their location, size and the time they were moved), so you can put them back. Entries are removed after 30 days, and you can clear the list at any time.</li>
      <li>Storage history: for each scan you keep, the total size and the size of each top-level folder, so you can see how your storage changes. You can clear it at any time.</li>
      <li>A small diagnostics log of crashes and errors (the time, Tessera's version and your operating system, with file and folder names removed), so a problem can be looked into if you choose to send it to us. It is never sent automatically. Settings &gt; Diagnostics shows where it is.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>When Tessera connects to the internet</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Licence checks.</strong> When you activate Tessera Pro, and every few days afterwards, Tessera sends your licence key and a general device label such as "Tessera on Windows" to our payment provider, Dodo Payments, to confirm the licence. Deactivating sends the same details.</li>
      <li><strong>Update check.</strong> Tessera can fetch a small public file from this website that lists the latest version. The request contains no information about you or your files beyond what any web request includes, such as your IP address. You can turn this off in Settings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Tessera has no analytics, no telemetry, no advertising and no automatic crash reporting. File names, folders and scan results are never sent anywhere.</p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>Purchases are processed by Dodo Payments, which acts as the merchant of record and handles payment, billing details and tax. We receive the order and licence details needed to provide and support your licence, such as your name, email address and country. We never receive or store your card details.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This website uses no cookies, analytics or tracking scripts. It is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which processes standard request information such as IP addresses to deliver and protect the site.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can clear the Recently moved list and storage history inside Tessera, deactivate your licence in Settings, and remove the app at any time. To ask about the information we hold about your purchase, or to have it corrected or deleted where the law allows, email us.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Beyond Enterprises, <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a></p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published here with a new effective date.</p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
